  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It is the evidence an auditor asks to see before accepting an entry.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It states what was supplied and what is now due.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The seller owes the reduction, so the seller issues the credit note.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The buyer uses it to claim a reduction he has not been allowed.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It evidences what was delivered, not what it cost.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The counterfoil records the payment written on the cheque.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It is signed by the person receiving the petty cash.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It is sent monthly for checking, not as a legal demand.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The sales day book lists credit sales from invoices issued.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Purchases day book lists credit purchases from invoices received.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Returns inwards is the book for goods coming back from customers.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Returns outwards covers goods the firm sends back.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Items outside the four day books go in the general journal.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It records cash transactions and also serves as the cash account.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It is the collection of accounts, each with a debit and a credit side.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    One account per person or firm, for debtors and creditors.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The total of credit sales raises debtors and is credited to sales.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Purchases rise and creditors rise by the total of credit purchases.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Each account contributes its balance, debit or credit.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Sales is income, so it carries a credit balance.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Purchases is an expense, so it carries a debit balance.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    An omission removes both entries, so the trial balance still agrees.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Debits exceed credits by ₦57,000, so the suspense account is credited and the trial balance difference is a debit.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The credit note reduces what the customer owes.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The receipt acknowledges payment received.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The buyer claims a reduction with a debit note.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The expense-like returns inwards account is debited and each debtor is credited.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The creditor's balance falls and returns outwards is credited.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Real accounts are for assets; rent, wages and sales are nominal accounts.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Nominal accounts record income and expenses.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It lists the balances produced by balancing off the accounts.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    An error of principle affects two accounts equally, so the totals still agree.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The signature proves receipt of the goods listed.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The wrong amount was entered first, in both accounts.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The purchase of a fixed asset on credit is not a purchase of goods for resale.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Each debtor has a personal account in the sales (debtors) ledger.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It checks that the debits and credits are equal.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Closing stock is an adjustment made in the final accounts, not a ledger balance.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Each transaction begins with a document and ends with a balance in the trial balance.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Returns inwards is debited and the individual debtors are credited.
  ]

]

